{
  "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
  "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case concerns a trademark dispute between Hetronic (a U. S. company) and six foreign parties (collectively Abitron). Hetronic manufactures remote controls for construction equipment. Abitron, once a licensed distributor for Hetronic, claimed ownership of the rights to much of Hetronic's intellectual property and began employing Hetronic's marks on products it sold."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "certiorari to the united states court of appeals for the tenth circuit No. 21\u20131043. Argued March 21, 2023\u2014Decided June 29, 2023"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0000-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "a jury later awarded Hetronic approximately $96 million in damages related to Abitron's global employment of Hetronic's marks."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Abitron",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Abitron contends that\n\u00a7 1114(1)(a) and \u00a7 1125(a)(1) focus on preventing infringing\nuse of trademarks, while Hetronic argues that they focus\nboth on protecting the goodwill of mark owners and on pre-\nventing consumer confusion. The United States as amicus\ncuriae argues that the provisions focus on only likely con-\nsumer confusion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Hetronic",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Hetronic argues that they focus both on protecting the goodwill of mark owners and on preventing consumer confusion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The United States as amicus curiae argues that the provisions focus on only likely consumer confusion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0001-0003",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In sum, we hold that \u00a7 1114(1)(a) and \u00a7 1125(a)(1) are not\nextraterritorial and that the infringing \u201cuse in commerce\u201d of\na trademark provides the dividing line between foreign and\ndomestic applications of these provisions. Under the Act,\nthe \u201cterm `use in commerce' means the bona fde use of a\nmark in the ordinary course of trade,\u201d where the mark\nserves to \u201cidentify and distinguish [the mark user's] goods\n. . . and to indicate the source of the goods.\u201d \u00a7 1127."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0001-0004",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I agree with the Court that 15 U. S. C. \u00a7 1114(1)(a) and\n\u00a7 1125(a)(1) do not apply extraterritorially. Ante, at 421. I\nalso agree that the \u201c `use in commerce' of a trademark\u201d that\nboth statutory sections describe \u201cprovides the dividing line\nbetween foreign and domestic applications\u201d of these provi-\nsions. Ante, at 428."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0002-0001",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Guided by this understanding of \u201cuse in commerce,\u201d I join the Court's opinion in full."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0002-0002",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "43(a)(1)(A) of the Lanham Act extends to activities carried out abroad when there is a likelihood of consumer confusion in the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioners argue that the focus of the statute is the \u201cuse\u201d of the mark \u201cin commerce.\u201d Brief for Petitioners 39."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent, by contrast, argues that the Act has two distinct focuses: protecting mark owners from reputational harm and protecting consumers from confusion. Brief for Respondent 45\u201348."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0002-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government, as amicus curiae supporting neither party, offers a middle ground. In its view, the focus of the statute is consumer confusion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0003-0000",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "in order for there to be a domestic application of a statute. Calling this requirement \u201cstraightforward,\u201d \u201cestablished precedent\u201d does not make it so. Ante, at 423, 425."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0003-0001",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court's analysis is also inconsistent with Steele. According to the Court, \u201cSteele implicated both domestic conduct and a likelihood of domestic confusion,\u201d so it offers no guidance in resolving this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0003-0003",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That principle recognizes that a trademark has separate legal existence in each country where the mark \u201cis registered or legally recognized.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0003-0004",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court's arguments about the impending \u201cinternational discord\u201d that will result from the Government's approach are simply overblown."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1043",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "372f0e4580b4a13e6a3ad449a750ba0ed78a79045fe07b17ef24ac032161be13",
      "evidence_id": "ev-372f0e4580b4-0003-0005",
      "kind": "concurrence",
      "opinion_part": "concurrence",
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Lanham Act covers petitioners' activities abroad so long as respondent can show that those activities are \u201clikely to cause confusion, or to cause mistake, or to deceive\u201d in the United States and can prove all elements necessary to establish liability under the Act."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
